Subject: [PATCH] usb: hub: run the hub workqueue at high priority
Upstream-Status: Pending

First car capture with 0047 and 0048 on the NAC Wave 2 - the first
role switch after boot succeeds now, for the first time:

  [1.092189] Port Connect Detected
  [1.092549] usb usb1-port1: OTG root port: connect debounce skipped   <- 0047/0048: 0.4ms
  [1.255234] Port Enable Changed (now 1)                               <- reset released, +163ms
  [1.467235] usb 1-1: new high-speed USB device number 2 using dwc2
  [1.492881] usb 1-1: New USB device found, idVendor=15a2, idProduct=1234
  [1.551458] iPhone: status -> accessory

The hub thread was on the port 0.4ms after the connect, but still took
113ms to assert the reset (released at +163ms, the pulse is 50ms), and
another 212ms from reset to the first descriptor where an idle system
takes 73ms. Everything in between is CPU contention: this happens at
1.1s after boot, alongside the aic8800 firmware upload with its md5
pass, RF calibration and the readahead sweep, on one core. The head
unit waits ~200ms from its own pull-up for the reset; we were at
~185ms. It worked, with the margin of a coin toss.

Enumeration is latency-bound work of a few hundred microseconds per
step, interleaved with waits. Run hub_wq as a WQ_HIGHPRI workqueue so
its worker gets the CPU ahead of the bulk work whenever it is
runnable. No behavioural change beyond scheduling priority; every USB
host in the tree enumerates the same way, just sooner under load.

Written against the letux-6.18.y tree at a3d00c045d89 with 0032 and
0047 applied. Not yet compiled or run.
---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -6089,7 +6089,15 @@
 	 * device was gone before the EHCI controller had handed its port
 	 * over to the companion full-speed controller.
 	 */
-	hub_wq = alloc_workqueue("usb_hub_wq", WQ_FREEZABLE, 0);
+	/*
+	 * WQ_HIGHPRI: on this single-core SoC the hub thread competes with
+	 * WiFi firmware upload, RF calibration and readahead right when the
+	 * head unit swaps roles and waits ~200ms for its bus reset. Measured
+	 * on a NAC Wave 2: 113ms from "Port Connect Detected" to the reset
+	 * being asserted under boot load, ~10ms when idle. Enumeration is
+	 * latency-bound, not throughput-bound; let it win the CPU.
+	 */
+	hub_wq = alloc_workqueue("usb_hub_wq", WQ_FREEZABLE | WQ_HIGHPRI, 0);
 	if (hub_wq)
 		return 0;
 
